        "problem": "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-(x-2)^{2}=1.$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-(x-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-(0-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-4 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5} & =5 \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =25 \\\\ y+5 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ y & =-10,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,-10)$ and $(0,0).$",
